 "power_notes": "Budgets are the real currents: VBUS_IN, VBUS and PVDD 5 A, the 28 V x 5 A PD contract (the firmware governor holds sustained input near 13 W, so 5 A is the peak); +5V 0.65 A (U5's 3V3 buck at the 0.3 A +3V3 budget, both amps' VDD, LP5907, +5VA, CH340C, the front board). Every layer's pour carries its budget on its own (check_current): In1/In2 are 1 oz, and kicad/gen/power_trunk.py cleared the GND stitch grid from the In2 power planes and reshaped their zones after planes_gen (the In2 regions here are the rectangles planes_gen lays; that script's ZONES are the outlines on the board). PVDD overrides: each F.Cu finger between an amp's output pins feeds one bridge, so at full stereo drive on Plus (U15 only) a finger carries half the 5 A, 2.5 A; the pin pitch fixes its 1.6-1.75 mm width, and its five vias into the In2 plane sit 1-4 mm from the pins. +5V overrides: the four layer changes on the branch to U2 (CH340C, ~20 mA) and J3 (two +5V pins to the Ultra front board: LCD backlight, LEDs, IR, ~0.2 A) are judged at 0.35 A, one via each; the trunk's layer changes have two. Track widths stay sized for the tracks that remain, plane taps and short stubs (the plane-fed rails' track findings are advisory), so kicad/core.kicad_dru keeps its width rules: re-running rules_gen from these budgets would ask every tap for trunk width, as it reads no plane_fed. The amp OUT/SPK nets (3.7 A rms continuous sine, 2 x 56 W governor-capped) ride the solid fan-in pours from kicad/gen/power_zones.py; check_irdrop covers those paths at P8.",
 "diff_pairs_note": "Explicitly empty. The USB full-speed pair (12 Mb/s) and the two 100BASE-TX pairs run about 10 mm, so coupling them adds nothing measurable, and the router doesn't couple pairs (route_critical's KRT diff pass shorted). They are routed as ordinary nets at the Default width."
}
